{"text":"kuruntokai","n":1,"lines":["செங்களம் படக்கொன் றவுணர்த் தேய்த்த","செங்கோ லம்பிற் செங்கோட்டி யானைக்","கழல்தொடிச் சேஎய் குன்றம்","குருதிப் பூவின் குலைக்காந் தட்டே"],"tr":["ceṅkaḷam paṭakkoṉ ṟavuṇart tēytta","ceṅkō lampiṟ ceṅkōṭṭi yāṉaik","kaḻaltoṭic cēey kuṉṟam","kurutip pūviṉ kulaikkān taṭṭē"],"colophon":{"tinai":"kuṟiñci","tinai_ta":"குறிஞ்சி","speaker_ta":"தோழி கூற்று","poet_ta":"திப்புத் தோளார்","speaker_en":"her friend (tōḻi)","poet_tr":"Tipput Tōḷār"},"scan":{"meter":"nēricai āciriyappā","ok":true,"checks":[{"name":"lines","ok":true,"detail":"4 lines"},{"name":"feet per line","ok":true,"detail":"3×4, 1×3 feet"},{"name":"foot types","ok":true,"detail":"iyaṟcīr 14, veṇcīr 1"},{"name":"linkage","ok":true,"detail":"āciriyattaḷai 8, veṇṭaḷai 6"},{"name":"ending","ok":true,"detail":"ends on ஏ"}],"ending":"ஏ","lines":[[{"text":"செங்களம்","tr":"ceṅkaḷam","foot":"kūviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"செங்","tr":"ceṅ"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"களம்","tr":"kaḷam"}]},{"text":"படக்கொன்","tr":"paṭakkoṉ","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"படக்","tr":"paṭak"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"கொன்","tr":"koṉ"}]},{"text":"றவுணர்த்","tr":"ṟavuṇart","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"றவு","tr":"ṟavu"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ணர்த்","tr":"ṇart"}]},{"text":"தேய்த்த","tr":"tēytta","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"தேய்த்","tr":"tēyt"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"த","tr":"ta"}]}],[{"text":"செங்கோ","tr":"ceṅkō","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"செங்","tr":"ceṅ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"கோ","tr":"kō"}]},{"text":"லம்பிற்","tr":"lampiṟ","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"லம்","tr":"lam"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"பிற்","tr":"piṟ"}]},{"text":"செங்கோட்டி","tr":"ceṅkōṭṭi","foot":"tēmāṅkāy","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"செங்","tr":"ceṅ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"கோட்","tr":"kōṭ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"டி","tr":"ṭi"}]},{"text":"யானைக்","tr":"yāṉaik","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"யா","tr":"yā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"னைக்","tr":"ṉaik"}]}],[{"text":"கழல்தொடிச்","tr":"kaḻaltoṭic","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"கழல்","tr":"kaḻal"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"தொடிச்","tr":"toṭic"}]},{"text":"சேஎய்","tr":"cēey","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"சே","tr":"cē"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"எய்","tr":"ey"}]},{"text":"குன்றம்","tr":"kuṉṟam","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"குன்","tr":"kuṉ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"றம்","tr":"ṟam"}]}],[{"text":"குருதிப்","tr":"kurutip","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"குரு","tr":"kuru"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"திப்","tr":"tip"}]},{"text":"பூவின்","tr":"pūviṉ","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"பூ","tr":"pū"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வின்","tr":"viṉ"}]},{"text":"குலைக்காந்","tr":"kulaikkān","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"குலைக்","tr":"kulaik"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"காந்","tr":"kān"}]},{"text":"தட்டே","tr":"taṭṭē","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"தட்","tr":"taṭ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"டே","tr":"ṭē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"செங்களம்","parts":[{"text":"செங்களம்","lemma":"செங்களம்","gloss":"red battlefield"}],"gloss":"red battlefield","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பட","parts":[{"text":"படு","lemma":"paṭu","gloss":"to fall"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to fall"},{"surface":"கொன்று","parts":[{"text":"கொன்று","lemma":"கொன்று","gloss":"having killed"}],"gloss":"having killed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அவுணர்","parts":[{"text":"அவுணர்","lemma":"avuṇar","gloss":"demons/Asuras"}],"gloss":"demons"},{"surface":"தேய்த்த","parts":[{"text":"தேய்","lemma":"tēy","gloss":"to wear down/destroy"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"t","gloss":"transitive marker"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"t","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"who destroyed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செங்கோல்","parts":[{"text":"செங்கோல்","lemma":"செங்கோல்","gloss":"straight-shafted"}],"gloss":"straight-shafted","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அம்பின்","parts":[{"text":"அம்பு","lemma":"ampu","gloss":"arrow"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"oblique/genitive suffix"}],"gloss":"of the arrow"},{"surface":"செங்கோட்டி","parts":[{"text":"செங்கோட்டி","lemma":"செங்கோட்டி","gloss":"having red tusks"}],"gloss":"having red tusks","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"யானை","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"yānai","gloss":"elephant"}],"gloss":"elephant"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கழல்","parts":[{"text":"கழல்","lemma":"kaḻal","gloss":"warrior's anklet"}],"gloss":"warrior's anklet"},{"surface":"தொடி","parts":[{"text":"தொடி","lemma":"toṭi","gloss":"armlet"}],"gloss":"armlet"},{"surface":"சேஎய்","parts":[{"text":"சேஎய்","lemma":"சேஎய்","gloss":"Lord Murugan"}],"gloss":"Lord Murugan","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"குன்றம்","parts":[{"text":"குன்றம்","lemma":"kuṉṟam","gloss":"hill"}],"gloss":"hill"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"குருதி","parts":[{"text":"குருதி","lemma":"kuruti","gloss":"blood"}],"gloss":"blood"},{"surface":"பூவின்","parts":[{"text":"பூ","lemma":"pū","gloss":"flower"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"genitive/oblique suffix"}],"gloss":"of the flower"},{"surface":"குலை","parts":[{"text":"குலை","lemma":"kulai","gloss":"cluster/bunch"}],"gloss":"cluster"},{"surface":"காந்தட்டே","parts":[{"text":"காந்தள்","lemma":"kāntal","gloss":"flame lily"},{"text":"து","lemma":"tu","gloss":"pronominal suffix"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"clitic of emphasis"}],"gloss":"is indeed the flame lily"}]}],"literal":"Red battlefield to fall, having killed, the demons who destroyed, / with straight-shafted arrows, with red-tusked elephants, / wearing warrior-anklets and armlets, Murugan's hill, / has clusters of flame lilies like blood-colored flowers.","translation":"The hill of Lord Murugan, who wears warrior-anklets and armlets, who destroyed the demons, killing them so they fell on the red battlefield, with his straight-shafted arrows and red-tusked elephants, is filled with clusters of flame lilies that look like flowers of blood.","modern":"செக்கச்சிவந்த போர்க்களத்தில் வீழுமாறு அசுரர்களைக் கொன்று அழித்த, செம்மையான தண்டையுடைய அம்புகளையும் செங்கோட்டு யானையையும் உடைய, வீரக்கழலும் தொடியும் அணிந்த முருகப் பெருமானுடைய மலையானது, குருதி போன்ற நிறமுடைய பூக்களைக் கொண்ட காந்தள் மலர்க் கொத்துக்களை உடையதாகும்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Kurinji (mountainous) landscape. The companion (தோழி) speaks of the hill belonging to Lord Murugan (Cēey), who is the patron deity of the Kurinji region. She describes his great battle where he destroyed the demons, turning the battlefield red with blood. The hill is filled with clusters of red flame lilies (kāntal) that resemble blood-red flowers, mirroring the imagery of the battlefield. This vivid red imagery connects the divine protector of the land with the natural beauty of the mountain, emphasizing the strength and passion associated with the region. The key words are 'சேஎய்' (Murugan), 'குன்றம்' (hill), and 'காந்தள்' (flame lily).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.8],[0.91,1.76],[1.82,2.0],[2.0,2.9],[3.05,3.2],[3.5,4.13],[4.13,4.2],[4.2,6.0],[6.0,6.2],[6.2,6.5],[6.5,8.2],[8.2,8.3],[8.3,8.87],[8.87,9.27]],"female":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,0.8],[1.12,1.6],[1.6,2.0],[2.0,2.94],[3.32,3.8],[3.8,4.34],[4.4,4.5],[4.5,6.3],[6.3,6.5],[6.5,6.9],[6.9,8.8],[8.8,8.9],[8.9,9.49],[9.49,9.7]]}}